<tr><td align=3D"left" class=3D"text" style=3D"background:#FFFFFF;font-size=
:0px;padding:0 16px;word-break:break-word;"><div style=3D"font-family:Georg=
ia, serif;font-size:16px;font-weight:400;line-height:22px;text-align:left;c=
olor:#121212;">
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">For an elite head coach who isn=E2=80=99t =
used to seeing his team lose, suffering a rare defeat on the weekend before=
 an international break is particularly hard to take. With the vast majorit=
y of your players hightailing it out of Dodge to rack up more air miles tha=
n Santa Claus across a decade=E2=80=99s worth of Christmas Eves, the chance=
 to quickly put things right simply isn=E2=80=99t an option. With the first=
 lull of the season set to be longer than any before, the potential for int=
rospection, self-flagellation and over-thinking has never been higher. Luck=
ily, Mikel Arteta has never struck Football Daily as the kind of intense, b=
rooding and meticulous perfectionist likely to spend the next 19 days beati=
ng himself up over <a href=3D"https://ablink.editorial.theguardian.com/ss/c=
/u001.Yw_JkLMEmFuifc_XG18IRyTNtZQ7fIEMgszcCSneHEBgtjhYSJYcaNsDra0BxnPg3RJ44=
Fso9uMyQxe28Dp72VUa-frxnpRGmJWyK1RXsYXS15zy0MHbmkayPdyx1qmO7rJKczGBVePBiNdn=
QvwhZ2RDgswD-DbbCmcBzC8rihu_IGKV9JVok-S3RLKwJA8euGgz7EIGG_nXYQnJwsmujcC4bo_=
Pqa7TFCVNM1u6vLtuBJCQO_rBs_lL5SY7Fl1DwUqUMB71Ufcsq6HnJpWXV7WrReNAT40o0wUy31=
J6T78/4u8/zdUDuFBiS-KFrgpszWWMYA/h28/h001.o3lIJSlIwtSrTyZqZG-EhkUPHjyhF0_ew=
y4P50sA2ro" style=3D"color: #0077B6;">the monstering his team suffered</a> =
from Brighton on Saturday. Whether it=E2=80=99s forlornly moving magnets ar=
ound a tactics board or walking Win the dog around Arsenal=E2=80=99s largel=
y-deserted training ground until her little legs are stumps, we=E2=80=99re =
confident the Arsenal boss=E2=80=99s every fleeting thought over the next t=
hree weeks will not be laser-focused on the manner in which the Seagulls vi=
ciously pecked his team of champions into submission and how best to ensure=
 such a humiliation is never repeated.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">Of course, while Arteta is sitting on a sw=
ing, gazing into the middle distance like a sad Pablo Escobar, Fabian H=C3=
=BCrzeler can afford to cut loose and enjoy his early-season hiatus by indu=
lging in his passion for padel, a sport which our older reader may not know=
 is a new-fangled version of tennis for people too lazy to run. Slovenlines=
s when it comes to busting a gut is certainly not an accusation that can be=
 levelled at the German=E2=80=99s players, who tore into Arsenal like a swa=
rm of angry bees and buzzed around them with such scrupulously-organised ch=
aos that after 90 minutes their 3-0 margin of victory seriously flattered t=
he beaten holders. =E2=80=9CExtremely disappointed,=E2=80=9D <a href=3D"htt=
ps://ablink.editorial.theguardian.com/ss/c/u001.Yw_JkLMEmFuifc_XG18IRyTNtZQ=
7fIEMgszcCSneHEBgtjhYSJYcaNsDra0BxnPgDn_dN_KUEm9JSpxRQsLSdp1FyVsSiFzF6JKNyC=
eYLcycy_xYXnokTwIbj0R2o2m82medAUR0-YIedofK90R0M9xznGild6EOODWYDBBeEboCZe3DD=
ZT7QBq9k7RG_WyHXOskc6h_EVKXiLEnuPN0CiLJKunLfo9dnvYRow1flLcX10IpXnEwZRlqqzRG=
o1cVd75DCfSSd3IppXDOUFjymuo-TOB4rtX3b86a2_THnTs/4u8/zdUDuFBiS-KFrgpszWWMYA/=
h29/h001.gOb4klG14IdY6hssN6mNLfE3tcbA7lv3vEjxCddBrMw" style=3D"color: #0077=
B6;">parped a shocked and awed Arteta</a> after seeing his players subjecte=
d to a rare humiliation. =E2=80=9CBut first I think we have to congratulate=
 Brighton for the victory. I think they deserve it, I think they were the b=
etter team.=E2=80=9D</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">Wearing natty azzurri blue vintage shirts =
against Arsenal to mark their 125th anniversary, it=E2=80=99s difficult to =
imagine Brighton have played better since being founded in 1901. In the ear=
ly Path=C3=A9 News years, their first team was peopled by club legends like=
 Peter Ward, Johnny Crumplin and a be-headbanded Steve Foster; the current =
lineup has a decidedly more cosmopolitan feel and, in the likes of Charalam=
pos Kostoulas, Luka Vuskovic and Diego G=C3=B3mez, boasts future Brighton i=
cons and subsequent, overpriced, Chelsea squad members. =E2=80=9CI want to =
say congratulations to this special club for the history, for everyone who =
has contributed in the past, for everyone who=E2=80=99s contributing in the=
 present,=E2=80=9D cooed H=C3=BCrzeler, after a special day on the south co=
ast. =E2=80=9CI think <a href=3D"https://ablink.editorial.theguardian.com/s=
s/c/u001.Yw_JkLMEmFuifc_XG18IRyTNtZQ7fIEMgszcCSneHEBgtjhYSJYcaNsDra0BxnPg38=
irkP9T9ZDC1gkIJQ0xvD7jj7XH4JpHVEiC3kpsxJoWxh0e2gash7lsy0ozd8m2erzK0nf4ISa7f=
6AMFVzq_SQb3CW69ZiAq9FfrGAf978PZp3tov72Z2KFTW4hTIApRqWcLGAtXN0DBPi9967p7na2=
i-AyijhCh0mJB782mn1ZPNFOMyfy3Cew2lrqNgN5ieVqywkIdf56xY1t3sK71cYHbsuq4XYeksB=
W9lr7wl1CzxD8gQ9Rrg5mbKBQpeKA/4u8/zdUDuFBiS-KFrgpszWWMYA/h30/h001.6qE2VtAFX=
gk2rTAcVJwjN5Ur9O-Qe9CUHdSq2WamXbA" style=3D"color: #0077B6;">the history o=
f this club</a> is very impressive and hopefully everyone can enjoy who has=
 been a part of our journey so far.=E2=80=9D H=C3=BCrzeler went on to say t=
hat he considered Saturday=E2=80=99s performance more important than the re=
sult. Over the coming weeks in London Colney, his Arsenal counterpart will =
be treating both with equal significance.</p>
